v3.2.26
Radon Player 3.2.26: A DJ that keeps it fresh
## 3.2.26: A DJ that keeps it fresh (Windows and Android)
- **Most played instead of favourites in the DJ:** the DJ's favourites set played your starred songs, which few people star, so it had little to pick from. It's now a Most played set (from everything, or from a playlist), picked at random from your top 150 most played that the DJ hasn't played lately, so it goes well down the list instead of playing the same few at the top.
- **No song again for 300 songs:** the DJ kept a song out for 20 of its sets, but a song in one kind of set (Most played, say) could still turn up in another (a mood set) soon after. Now the DJ counts the last 300 songs it played, and none of them comes back in any set until 300 others have played; then it can again. The count starts with this update. Playing from a playlist with fewer songs than that, the ones played longest ago come back first.
- **Every DJ set, wherever the DJ plays from:** playing from a playlist, folder or album, the DJ only had a handful of kinds of set. Now it has every kind it has playing from everything (On repeat, Rediscover, On this day, Decade trip, Never skipped, Streaks, an album moment, an artist spotlight, the mood sets and the rest), made from only that playlist's songs, as well as the ones made for it (Not played yet, One artist, Mix). With new songs on, the new-song sets (New for you, More like this, Artists for you, Deep cuts) go by the playlist's songs and artists. A kind with too few of the playlist's songs is skipped until it has enough.
- **The DJ never stops between sets:** now and then the music stopped at the end of a set until you skipped (with the headphones, say), when the next set or its first song didn't start. Now if, a few seconds after a song ends, nothing's playing (no line being said, no set still being picked, and you didn't pause), the DJ goes on by itself: on to the next song or a new set, and a note in Problems says it happened.
- **A DJ set for every mood:** the DJ's mood set said it was playing "the mood you've been in", but the app only knows the songs' moods, not yours, and it picked the mood you play most nearly every time (Energetic, say). Now there are seven mood sets, moods alike together: Energetic, Party & Hype; Happy, Chill & Calm; Dreamy; Focus; Romantic; Sad & Dark; and Intense. Each takes its turn like any other set, and the DJ says what it's doing: "Hey, let's switch it up. We're going to play some happy, chill songs." The DJ's facts about moods now talk about what you've played, not what mood you're in.
- **The DJ never plays the same kind of set again too soon:** every kind of set (Most played, a mood, throwbacks…) now gets its turn before any comes back, the one played longest ago first. The DJ remembers this across everything: switching it to a playlist (its Most played is the same kind as yours), turning it off, or closing the app no longer starts it over with the same sets in the same order.
- **The DJ goes on with Repeat on:** with Repeat all on, the end of each DJ set went back to the first song the DJ played instead of on to the next set, and with Repeat off (and more than one queue) skipping past a set's last song went to your next queue. Now the DJ always goes on to a new set, for as long as it's on, never to another queue or back to its start: with the DJ, Repeat goes between Repeat one (play the song again, then the DJ carries on) and off, and starting the DJ turns Repeat all off. Shuffle and Autoplay (∞) aren't used with the DJ either (they say so): the DJ plays each set in its own order and makes the next set itself, and Autoplay's songs never get added to the DJ's queue.

### Good to know
- **Android:** install RadonPlayer-Next.apk over Radon Player Next (same app, same signature: your library, settings and stats stay), or tap Update in Settings.
- **Windows:** Radon-Player-3.2.26.msi installs over 3.2.25, or use Update in Settings.
